# =============================================================================
# release-notifier — NotifierService (Connect, no authentication)
#
#   make api-check   validate every path below against api/proto
#   make api-notifier open this file (nvim) — see docs/http-collections.md
#
# release-notifier mounts these procedures WITHOUT an authentication or
# authorization interceptor (cmd/notifier/main.go), so no credential is needed —
# and none is checked. That is a registered gap, not a convenience:
#   - TASK-096 covers the inbound authentication + the egress allowlist;
#   - SECURITY.md §3.11 records that a caller can turn the control plane into an
#     HTTP client for an arbitrary URL.
# Only the read-only GetStatus is pre-filled; Send is listed, not armed.
# =============================================================================

### GetStatus (read-only; unauthenticated by design today)
# @name GetStatus
# @kulala-expect-status-code 200
POST {{NOTIFIER_URL}}/notifier.v1.NotifierService/GetStatus
Content-Type: application/json

{}

# Send enqueues a delivery job to a caller-supplied recipient — the SSRF surface
# TASK-096 closes. Body shape:
#   POST {{NOTIFIER_URL}}/notifier.v1.NotifierService/Send
#   {"operationId": "...", "channel": "NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL_WEBHOOK",
#    "recipient": "https://example.invalid/hook", "metadata": {}}
